WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.007
When did your team start each interview, and how long ago was it?

2
00:00:05.007 --> 00:00:09.538
In this lesson, you will learn to extract the time, hour, minute and second,

3
00:00:09.538 --> 00:00:13.422
find the earliest and latest time, and calculate age from a date.

4
00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:15.040
Let's look at the clock!

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.965
On the Transform tab, open the Time menu.

6
00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:24.562
Time Only keeps just the time part of a date time value.

7
00:00:24.562 --> 00:00:29.160
Here, the end column now shows only times like nine twenty AM.

8
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.074
Hour pulls out the hour as a number.

9
00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:35.414
Minute and Second work the same way.

10
00:00:35.414 --> 00:00:39.760
Use them to see, for example, which hours of the day interviews ended.

11
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.476
The Time menu also offers Earliest and Latest.

12
00:01:14.476 --> 00:01:19.858
Earliest returns the first time in the column, and Latest returns the last one,

13
00:01:19.858 --> 00:01:21.780
here twenty three fifty nine.

14
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.880
Both return a single value and replace the table, so I delete those steps

15
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.480
to get the table back.

16
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.207
Now, Age.

17
00:02:12.207 --> 00:02:15.837
Select the start column, open Date, and choose Age.

18
00:02:15.837 --> 00:02:21.080
Power Query calculates how much time has passed between each date and today.

19
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.580
The result is a duration, which looks like days, hours, minutes and seconds.

20
00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:36.760
To make it readable, open Duration and choose Total Days, or Total Years.

21
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.695
Now each row shows the number of days since the interview.

22
00:02:50.695 --> 00:02:55.380
The Duration menu also has Days, Hours, Minutes, Total Hours, and more.

23
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.280
Age is great for checking how old your data is, or how many days

24
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.720
a case has stayed open. Keep practicing!

